#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0378 expect=violation domain=TT
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE SYMMETRY PIN (Fix #294 / M3-D15(ii)). The TTENRL column is REMOVED and TTDUR is blank on both rows, so NEITHER variable is present for either Stage -- the most complete form of the defect. Before M3-D15 the Check read `empty(TTENRL) and (not var_exists(\"TTDUR\") or empty(TTDUR))`: the TTDUR half was authored TOLERANT of absence while the TTENRL half was a bare leaf that NonEmptyGuardInliner armed with var_exists(\"TTENRL\"), so the two halves of an either-or pair of EQUAL standing behaved oppositely and this dataset was SILENT. Authoring the TTENRL half the same way makes the shipped Check symmetric; the shape is not novel (fda/FDA-SE2307 is the same either-or family, tolerant on both halves)."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 RSTGCD=ST1
#expectViolationAt row=2 RSTGCD=ST2
dataset TT class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Repro Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RSTGCD  type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
col RSTAGE  type=Char label="Description of Repro Stage"
col TTDUR   type=Char label="Duration of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | TT | ST1 | Premating | 
S1 | TT | ST2 | Gestation | 
---
